# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Two jobs, and the second one matters more than it looks.
#
# 1. Keeping the build correct. The images install dependencies themselves, for Linux. Copying the
#    host's `node_modules` in on top of that replaces a working install with one built for another
#    platform â€” and under pnpm on Windows, with symlinks that point at paths the container has never
#    heard of. That is what made the first build of these images fail.
#
# 2. Keeping secrets out of the image. Every file in the context can end up in a layer, and layers
#    are kept even when a later step deletes the file. A Firebase Admin service account key is a
#    private key for the whole project; an image that carries one is a credential leak the moment it
#    is pushed to any registry. Credentials reach a running container as environment variables, and
#    never as a file in the build.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore where the two agree; the secrets block below is deliberately identical to it,
# because anything unsafe to commit is unsafe to ship in an image.

# --- dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
dist-worker/
**/dist-worker/
build/
**/build/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
coverage/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
secrets/
google-credentials.json
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- the mobile app ----------------------------------------------------------
# Neither server image serves Flutter, and its build output is the largest thing in the repo.
apps/mobile/

# --- local-only infrastructure ----------------------------------------------
infra/.data/
infra/docker-compose.yml

# --- everything else that only slows the context down ------------------------
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
docs/
*.md
!apps/*/README.md
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
